// COMPOSITION — House creates and owns its Rooms
class Room:
    method Room(label):
        this.label = label

class House:
    method House(numRooms):
        this.rooms = []
        for i in 1..numRooms:
            this.rooms.append(new Room("Room " + i))   // created internally
    // destroying House destroys its rooms too — no other owner exists


// AGGREGATION — Department holds Professors it does not create
class Professor:
    method Professor(name):
        this.name = name

class Department:
    method Department(name):
        this.name = name
        this.professors = []

    method addProfessor(prof):
        this.professors.append(prof)   // passed in, not built here

p1 = new Professor("Dr. Rao")
cs = new Department("CS")
cs.addProfessor(p1)
// deleting cs leaves p1 alive — it can join another department
```

The tell: composition calls `new` **inside** the owner; aggregation receives an **already-built** object from outside.
